      "writtenOn": "2026-04-30T13:17:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The flash_em32_check_bank_protected() helper does not introduce or emulate\na separate sector‑based protection mechanism.\n\nIt **does** emulate sector based protection. It hides implementation details e.g. what if the \"sector\" is partialy protected.\n\n\u003e EC flash APIs are bank‑oriented\n\nYes, this is correct, but the emulation should happen **in this driver**, not in your private library.\n\nThe consequence of your design is that write protection check before writing/erasing rebuilds the protection range in a very expensive way. It would be much simpler if you could take protection ranges and check if requested write/erase falls in that.",
      "parentUuid": "33441e10_2c8c4153",
