      "writtenOn": "2026-05-04T07:00:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the detailed explanation, I understand your concern.\n\nYou’re right that exposing only a bank‑level helper means the cros_flash\ndriver needs to iterate and effectively reconstruct the protection range\nwhen checking write/erase requests, which is both less clear and more\nexpensive than working directly with explicit ranges.\n\nIn this CL, this is the first introduction of flash write‑protection\nsupport on this platform, together with the initial private library.\nThe current bank‑based query was chosen to get correct and safe protection\nsemantics working end‑to‑end with existing EC bank‑oriented APIs.\n\nI agree that a cleaner long‑term model would be to expose protection ranges\n(start/end) from the library, and perform all range‑to‑bank mapping and\npolicy checks in the cros_flash driver itself (including write/erase and\nstate reporting paths).\n\nGiven that, would you prefer to do that refactor as part of this CL, or\nwould it be acceptable to address it in a follow‑up change to keep the\nscope of this one focused?",
